= Maintaining Your FujiNet Cartridge

Your FujiNet cartridge should bring many years of enjoyment. To keep it in
good working condition, please remember the following points:

#grid(columns: (1fr, 1fr), column-gutter: 14pt, [
- Always turn the console’s POWER OFF before putting the cartridge in or
  taking it out.
- Do not try to force the cartridge into the console.
- Do not push anything into the three small service holes on the cartridge.
- Push the memory card straight in and let it spring straight out. Do not
  pry at it.
], [
- Use only a USB-C phone charger or a computer’s USB port in the USB-C
  socket.
- Do not spill liquids on the cartridge or pour them into the console’s
  slot.
- Do not drop the cartridge or leave it in great heat.
- Clean the outside of the cartridge with a soft, slightly damp cloth.
])

== Keeping FujiNet Up to Date

FujiNet’s firmware -- the programs inside the cartridge -- is improved all the
time. New versions, and how to load them, are announced at *fujinet.online*.
Loading new firmware does not change your hosts or your WiFi settings.
